{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-2021"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of pesticides and other agrochemical products"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "2021"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :pesticide-agrochemical/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :consumer-safety :environmental-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :pesticide-agrochemical-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae :cfd]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "PesticideAdvisor ⊣ Pesticide & Agrochemical Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor for pesticide and other agrochemical product
 manufacturing (formulation/mixing and packaging lines producing
 herbicides, insecticides, fungicides, rodenticides, nematicides,
 molluscicides, fumigants, plant-growth regulators, desiccants/
 defoliants, and tank-mix adjuvants) -- not direct formulation/mixing-
 line-equipment control authority, and NOT a pesticide-registration or
 label-approval authority. Four ops (`:log-production-batch` /
 `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-safety-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Twelve concrete
 governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD invariants:
 propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect
 allowlist (no direct formulation/mixing-line-equipment control),
 permanent line-actuate block, permanent pesticide-registration/
 label-approval-authority-decision block, independent equipment
 verification/registration before maintenance scheduling, independent
 batch verification/registration before shipment coordination,
 independent shipment-weight recompute against the batch's own logged
 weight, double-schedule guard, product-type validation,
 active-ingredient-concentration plausibility validation, and
 active-ingredient-concentration label-ceiling validation (modeled on
 representative EPA/PMRA maximum labeled active-ingredient
 concentration ranges per product category). Safety-concern flagging
 (chemical-hazard toxicity/exposure-risk/environmental-contamination)
 ALWAYS escalates to a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch`
 is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
 governor-clean."}
